my name's andrew evans and i was  infected through hemophilia treatment at  the age of five with hiv and hepatitis c  i developed full-blown aids at the age  of 16 and barely managed to survive to  the age of 20. andrew is one of an  estimated 4 000 victims who survived  what's been labeled the worst treatment  disaster in nhs history where patients  were infected with hiv and hepatitis c  through contaminated blood products it's  thought around 2400 people died many  suffered in silence because of public  attitudes to hiv the stigma was still so  strong against those people  frightened me to death  and so i kept everything completely  under wraps as far as that was concerned  i told nobody at school  um  i didn't tell even my best friends about  it  um until it became absolutely apparent  that there was  you know something going on that i was  ill and i couldn't hide it anymore  social care shall be the truth shall be  the truth after decades of campaigning  an inquiry was launched in 2018  former health secretaries and a prime  minister gave evidence no one accepting  blame or the argument for compensation  what had happened to them was  incredibly  bad luck  but campaigners say it was incompetence  reckless blood collecting methods in the  u.s and a lack of checks when imported  to the uk  the inquiries recommended compensation  and now the government has announced  each victim will get a hundred thousand  pounds obviously it's a very welcome sum  of money  if you split 100 000 pounds over 40  years of being infected it's two and a  half thousand pounds a year it will help  at the moment  for me personally to do  what i want to do most which is to  secure my family's future but i'm also  very aware of the people this doesn't  deal with at the moment  i'm lauren denise palmer and i  lost my both my parents  back when i was nine years old lauren  was orphaned by the scandal her father  was given infected blood and died of  aids in august 1993 he unknowingly  infected her mother who died in the same  month  while spouses of victims will get  compensation parents who lost children  or children who lost their parents won't  get paid  how can they have this differentiation  and this hierarchy between bereaved  families  i mean all their lives matter just as  much as the next person i haven't been  able to lead a normal life as such where  i've got the stability of having two  parents  for support and  to go through education and go to uni  uh  be able to stay at home long enough to  save to put a deposit on a on a home so  i haven't  haven't done any of that  this is a victory for people like andrew  but decades late and many like lauren  who've suffered are still waiting for  recognition jason farrell sky news
 

